<title>USA: UPS delivering 10 pct of normal volume.</title>
<headline>UPS delivering 10 pct of normal volume.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>UPS said Tuesday that it delivered about ten percent of its normal daily volume of 12 million packages on Monday, using 50,000 management and administrative employees.</p>
<p>The company also said it is continuing to petition the White House to end the strike, citing the &quot;considerable&quot; economic consequences of the nationwide work stoppage.</p>
<p>The president has the power under the Taft-Hartley Act to intervene in the strike, said the company, though it is rarely used and generally chosen only as a last resort.</p>
<p>The company said the last time the Taft-Hartley Act was invoked was in the 1970s.</p>
</text>
